WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.458 --> 00:00:06.250
When you sign with the Spurs,

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:10.541
your soul and your personality are put into the box.

00:00:11.708 --> 00:00:15.541
There will be a new king in the East

00:00:19.833 --> 00:00:21.291
It is your time

00:00:23.708 --> 00:00:26.833
Spurs of the East

00:00:56.791 --> 00:00:57.708
Your Grace?

00:00:58.083 --> 00:01:00.500
You wanted to see me?

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:01.833
Yes

00:01:03.958 --> 00:01:08.000
I like to pretend they’re…little eggs

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:09.583
You see, the lower houses,

00:01:09.583 --> 00:01:12.083
they are the hens.

00:01:12.083 --> 00:01:13.583
And I...

00:01:13.583 --> 00:01:16.750
am the fox that snatches their little babies.

00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:18.791
You’ve collected so many… 

00:01:18.791 --> 00:01:21.000
So much talent

00:01:21.958 --> 00:01:23.958
almost, uh, too much

00:01:23.958 --> 00:01:26.958
In Bostonia, there is no such thing as too much.

00:01:26.958 --> 00:01:27.625
I know one thing

00:01:27.625 --> 00:01:30.083
Lord Pop would have never lost control of this house

00:01:30.083 --> 00:01:32.333
Pfft...Spurs of the East...

00:01:32.333 --> 00:01:33.375
Lucky for you, 

00:01:33.375 --> 00:01:36.083
there’s one last road trip before the tournament starts.

00:01:36.083 --> 00:01:37.541
I suggest you find a way

00:01:37.541 --> 00:01:40.541
to get our knights on the same page.

00:01:40.541 --> 00:01:42.000
Or else…

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:44.791
You would never. This city loves me.

00:01:44.791 --> 00:01:47.416
Like they loved The King in the Fourth?

00:01:47.416 --> 00:01:48.333
Get it done

00:01:56.958 --> 00:01:59.666
Unbelievable we gotta share a tent with the rotation guys

00:01:59.666 --> 00:02:01.166
We was the heroes last year!

00:02:01.166 --> 00:02:03.416
If you’re feeling cramped, expand your mind

00:02:03.416 --> 00:02:06.166
Squires these days...so entitled

00:02:06.166 --> 00:02:07.916
Better stop calling us squires, Marcus

00:02:07.916 --> 00:02:09.958
You don’t scare me, Terry

00:02:09.958 --> 00:02:11.416
You think you’re some wise veteran— 

00:02:13.666 --> 00:02:14.625
What is that?

00:02:14.625 --> 00:02:18.416
I’ve seen that before. That there is a Soul Box.

00:02:18.416 --> 00:02:20.625
When you sign with House Spurs,

00:02:20.625 --> 00:02:24.208
your soul and personality go into that box.

00:02:24.208 --> 00:02:27.125
So it’s like a…Spurs culture thing?

00:02:27.125 --> 00:02:28.791
I didn’t want it to come to this 

00:02:28.791 --> 00:02:30.791
but there is too much talent here in this room

00:02:30.791 --> 00:02:33.166
for us to be treading water in the fourth seed.

00:02:33.166 --> 00:02:36.958
The Soul Box will help us contain our emotions and our egos,

00:02:36.958 --> 00:02:39.125
so that this group can reach its potential.

00:02:39.125 --> 00:02:41.375
Also makes you dull as dirt

00:02:41.375 --> 00:02:45.166
That thing's the reason nobody heard of me in San Antonio

00:02:45.166 --> 00:02:46.875
Oh, yeah. That’s the reason.

00:02:46.875 --> 00:02:48.375
I’ll do it

00:02:48.958 --> 00:02:50.125
All right, Al

00:02:50.125 --> 00:02:52.666
I want you to close your eyes and place your hand on the box

00:02:53.833 --> 00:02:55.458
Ser Al Horford,

00:02:55.458 --> 00:02:57.041
do you hereby commit fully, 

00:02:57.041 --> 00:03:01.291
to sacrifice your soul for the good of House Celtics?

00:03:01.916 --> 00:03:02.791
Aye

00:03:08.291 --> 00:03:09.416
So did it work or what?

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:12.875
He didn’t flinch!

00:03:13.166 --> 00:03:16.625
All right, who’s next? Anyone?

00:03:17.416 --> 00:03:18.500
I’ll do it

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:19.250
OK, no. Lucky—

00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:21.250
Gimme that box. I’ll do it.

00:03:21.250 --> 00:03:23.291
-Put my soul right in that box
-Thanks, Lucky, but this is for knights

00:03:24.250 --> 00:03:25.666
Marcus the Smart?

00:03:25.666 --> 00:03:30.458
I…I can’t. I’m sorry. My whole game is about emotion.

00:03:31.208 --> 00:03:31.916
Jaylen?

00:03:31.916 --> 00:03:34.583
Uh, I’m just worried about my brand is all

00:03:34.583 --> 00:03:36.000
What about you, Kyrie?

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:40.166
Ha, subjugate the light of my soul to your rectangular prism?

00:03:40.166 --> 00:03:41.750
No way... 

00:03:41.750 --> 00:03:43.125
I can’t even commit to next year

00:03:43.125 --> 00:03:44.541
Wow...what a leader

00:03:44.541 --> 00:03:46.125
OK, then why don’t you do it?

00:03:46.125 --> 00:03:46.958
Well, I just...

00:03:46.958 --> 00:03:49.625
don’t want to jeopardize my Mamba Mentality is all.

00:03:49.625 --> 00:03:52.125
Yeah, gods forbid you stop shooting 20-footers

00:03:52.125 --> 00:03:52.500
Yeah, gods forbid you stop shooting 20-footers

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:53.291
Oh, please. You’re one to talk.

00:03:53.291 --> 00:03:55.208
-Oh, I’m Jayson Tatum. I’m the man.
-Very funny.

00:03:55.208 --> 00:03:56.875
I’m going to House Pelicans to be the man!

00:03:56.875 --> 00:03:58.541
All right, guys. Come on!

00:03:58.541 --> 00:04:01.833
You know what? Clearly, this was a bad idea, OK?

00:04:01.833 --> 00:04:05.041
You guys are obviously not the Spurs,

00:04:05.041 --> 00:04:07.875
and I am clearly...not Lord Pop.

00:04:07.875 --> 00:04:10.500
No...you’re not

00:04:14.416 --> 00:04:16.250
You’re Brad Stevens. 

00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:18.791
The best X’s and O’s man I’ve ever known

00:04:18.791 --> 00:04:21.958
Yeah, nobody can write out-of-timeout plays like you

00:04:21.958 --> 00:04:23.541
Yeah, well, unfortunately,

00:04:23.541 --> 00:04:26.625
there’s no timeout long enough for me to fix all of THIS team’s issues.

00:04:28.666 --> 00:04:29.958
But what if there was

00:04:29.958 --> 00:04:30.916
Who said that?

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:33.250
The Time Lord…

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:35.500
Wait, ‘Time Lord'? I thought that was just a nickname. 

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:35.541
Wait, ‘Time Lord'? I thought that was just a nickname. 

00:04:35.541 --> 00:04:38.041
There’s a lot of things people don’t know about me

00:04:38.041 --> 00:04:38.958
Don’t get enough minutes

00:04:38.958 --> 00:04:40.208
Tell me about it

00:04:40.208 --> 00:04:44.291
But I’m pretty versatile. I can rebound, I can block,

00:04:44.291 --> 00:04:45.333
and I can stop time.

00:04:45.333 --> 00:04:47.125
Where’d you learn how to do that? 

00:04:47.125 --> 00:04:48.583
Texas A&amp;M

00:04:48.583 --> 00:04:50.333
But you were only there for two years!

00:04:50.333 --> 00:04:51.916
...or was I?

00:04:51.916 --> 00:04:53.833
Whoa

00:04:53.833 --> 00:04:56.583
So how does one just...stop time? 

00:04:56.583 --> 00:04:57.875
Just asking questions here

00:04:57.875 --> 00:05:01.291
It's a magic potion…called So’Da

00:05:02.291 --> 00:05:05.291
Banned in the realm since Jason Kidd used it against House Lakers,

00:05:05.291 --> 00:05:07.750
late in a battle when he had no timeouts left.

00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:10.416
Exactly how long are we talking about here?

00:05:10.416 --> 00:05:11.666
It will last till either you've

00:05:11.666 --> 00:05:13.750
come up with a way to solve our problems…

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:15.916
or 34 years...whichever comes first

00:05:15.916 --> 00:05:17.708
Why 34?

00:05:17.708 --> 00:05:19.208
It’s the Truth… 

00:05:19.208 --> 00:05:20.916
34 is the Truth’s number

00:05:20.916 --> 00:05:22.791
The guy who’s worse than Dwyane Wade!

00:05:22.791 --> 00:05:25.125
Actually, no. That’s just how much So'Da I have.

00:05:25.125 --> 00:05:26.833
All right, you’ve got this, Lord Commander! 

00:05:26.833 --> 00:05:27.708
Yeah! 

00:05:27.708 --> 00:05:30.208
-You’re Brad Stevens! 
-You’re a freaking genius!
-You're smartest in the realm!

00:05:30.208 --> 00:05:31.416
We know you can do this, Lord Commander!

00:05:31.416 --> 00:05:32.708
Are you all mad?

00:05:32.708 --> 00:05:35.708
Do you really think he can just come up with some

00:05:35.708 --> 00:05:39.375
magical out-of-timeout play that’s gonna fix all of our chemistry issues?

00:05:39.375 --> 00:05:41.916
Yeah, you know what? I do.

00:05:42.875 --> 00:05:45.458
Because I’m Brad F--king Stevens

00:05:48.375 --> 00:05:50.250
Time Lord, ready when you are

00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:52.291
All right

00:05:52.291 --> 00:05:54.416
Time...

00:05:54.416 --> 00:05:54.833
OUT

00:05:54.833 --> 00:05:55.541
OH  F--K

00:05:56.500 --> 00:05:58.333
Lord Commander? 

00:05:58.333 --> 00:05:59.291
You look like you’ve aged—

00:05:59.291 --> 00:06:01.125
34 years. Yep.

00:06:01.125 --> 00:06:03.041
So you...you didn’t...?

00:06:03.041 --> 00:06:04.291
Nope

00:06:04.291 --> 00:06:06.166
So, what’s all that?

00:06:06.166 --> 00:06:09.708
Mostly just gibberish. I gave up 20 ago, actually.

00:06:10.208 --> 00:06:11.208
What’s THAT?

00:06:13.541 --> 00:06:15.250
All right,

00:06:15.250 --> 00:06:19.916
I’ve got some good news and some bad news.

00:06:19.916 --> 00:06:22.291
Bad news first

00:06:22.291 --> 00:06:25.583
Lucky got frozen in time with me

00:06:27.541 --> 00:06:28.958
The So'Da spilled on him

00:06:28.958 --> 00:06:31.041
Oh, no. What have I—

00:06:31.041 --> 00:06:32.333
Unfortunately for Lucky, 

00:06:32.333 --> 00:06:36.083
he swore a blood oath to always perform during timeouts,

00:06:36.083 --> 00:06:39.833
obviously never thinking he’d, well...yeah.

00:06:41.208 --> 00:06:45.000
But he kept performing. He was juggling. Dancing.

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:47.083
Doing those wacky dunks

00:06:47.083 --> 00:06:49.875
Man, was he funny

00:06:49.875 --> 00:06:54.041
By year two, he was mostly performing stuff that could be done from a chair,

00:06:54.041 --> 00:06:58.750
like balancing bowls, singing, whatever.

00:06:58.750 --> 00:07:02.208
It was around year three where...he stopped talking

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:08.041
He was just miming and deliriously flailing his arms

00:07:08.083 --> 00:07:10.833
By year four, I thought he was doing this long bit 

00:07:10.833 --> 00:07:12.583
where he would just play dead.

00:07:12.583 --> 00:07:15.833
By year five, I realized...

00:07:16.458 --> 00:07:17.833
it wasn't a bit.

00:07:21.041 --> 00:07:22.958
So, um...

00:07:22.958 --> 00:07:24.291
what’s the good news?

00:07:24.291 --> 00:07:27.291
Well, I came up with a few pretty clever inbound plays

00:07:27.291 --> 00:07:28.916
that might get us to the second round.

00:07:53.875 --> 00:07:56.791
So, if you subscribe to Bleacher Report, 

00:07:56.791 --> 00:07:59.958
you can get notified any time a new Game of Zones comes out.

00:07:59.958 --> 00:08:01.541
And, can I comment, "first"?

00:08:01.541 --> 00:08:02.708
Yes, anything

00:08:02.708 --> 00:08:04.875
Even though I'm clearly not the first commenter? 

00:08:04.875 --> 00:08:06.208
Oh, whatever you want,

00:08:06.208 --> 00:08:08.000
as long as you follow the community guidelines.

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:09.833
Wait! Stop! Stop!

00:08:09.833 --> 00:08:13.583
He saw us! He saw us subscribing! 

